  "id": "COMPOUND:29932 - PROTEIN:6306",
  "verbalization": "Picrinine is shown to interact with Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, which is a target of multiple compounds, including (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan, 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide, and 2-Methylheptyl propanoate. All these compounds are known to inhibit the target enzyme CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, suggesting a common mechanism of action involving the inhibition of this enzyme. The evidence supports a potential pathway where Picrinine may act through a similar mechanism, targeting the same enzyme or a downstream pathway. The final score of 0.5502 indicates a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but further validation would be needed to confirm the direct interaction between Picrinine and the enzyme.",
